Release 6.0.0. Pins package-v0.10.0. Introducing Big Picture Mode for the Portal in short BPM

Changelog: 21-10-2026 12:01:48

Added. The intro of Suite Big Picture Mode draws the portal's icon from a 1024 px picture
(images/bc250-bazzite-suite-1024.webp), larger than before and scaled once to the screen's own pixels, and switching
back to Suite Desktop Mode plays the start-up swoosh again (owner, 21-10-2026).

Changelog: 21-10-2026 11:31:43

Fixed. Suite Big Picture Mode (owner, 21-10-2026): the orange local-build banner shows in it too, and so do all the
header's pills, the same ones as in Suite Desktop Mode (the window's row moves under the title and back): the focus
reaches them with up from the top row of icons, and A or Enter presses one. The mode pill reads Desktop or BPM mode,
and the dedicated Sound and mode pills of the mode are gone. An install or an update leaves the mode for the desktop,
where its terminal opens. The start-up swoosh has more bass and little above 2 kHz.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 11:22:52

Fixed. Suite Big Picture Mode (owner, 21-10-2026): the mode pill reads BPM mode and is as wide as the Sound pill, so its
text is no longer cut off; the line under the title is a short one per category, and ends in … where a screen is too
narrow for it. The icons are drawn from the 512 px icon of their category (portal/images/categories/, written by
tools/sync_icons.py), scaled once to the screen's own pixels, instead of the 256 px tile.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 11:08:05

Added. The portal fits a 1280 px handheld screen, the Steam Deck's (1280 x 800) and the ROG Xbox Ally X's (1280 x 720
with the desktop's scaling) (owner, 21-10-2026). The header's pills are in one row where there is room, else in
rows of about equal length, so the window is no longer 1390 px wide at least; the window opens at most as wide as the
screen. Suite Big Picture Mode draws its icons, type and header smaller on a screen under 1000 px high, swipes with a
finger.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 10:55:32

Added. Sound and Suite Big Picture Mode (owner, 21-10-2026). A swoosh plays when the portal opens; the new Sound pill
(Yes or No, kept) switches it and the mode's sound off, and without an audio output it is disabled and the portal
silent. The new Suite mode pill, and F11, switch between Suite Desktop Mode, the window as it was, and Suite Big
Picture Mode: fullscreen, with large icons and type, a category strip, and a focus that moves with the arrow keys or
a controller (d-pad, left stick, A, B, LB/RB, Y). It opens with a short animated intro with a futuristic sound; any
key, click or button skips it. The portal remembers the last mode and opens in it, and keeps the desktop window's
size, not the screen's. The sounds are made by tools/make_portal_sounds.py. The controller is read with pygame-ce,
which the portal's requirements add to the suite's venv; the portal listens to it only while its window has the
focus. The wallpaper's drawing moved to looks.py, unchanged.

