Changelog: 19-10-2026 16:58:45

Release 3.2.0. Pins mtool-v0.1.13.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 16:45:13

Added. The header shows the suite's stage beside the version, a Beta pill whose tooltip says what it means: the
suite is in active development, and features and layout may still change between releases. STAGE and STAGE_NOTE
in bc250_portal/__init__.py set it (the owner, 19-10-2026); STAGE = "" hides the pill. The version numbers stay
plain x.y.z. Tests: tests/test_window.py.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 16:36:08

Added. Media Tool (was Simple Demo Tool) is listed as [apps.mtool] (was [apps.dtool]), after the tool's move to
apps/mtool; its tile icon is images/apps/mtool.webp, its launcher ~/.local/bin/media-tool. The entry pins the first
release under its new tag prefix (mtool-v0.1.13) without a checksum until that release exists, which an app release
accepts and a portal release waits for. The record of a copy installed under dtool or demo-tool moves to the new
key when the portal starts. The Desktop icons setting counts media-tool.desktop as the suite's (was
simple-demo-tool.desktop).

Changelog: 19-10-2026 04:02:15

Release 3.1.0. Pins check-v0.5.0, helixsr-v0.4.0, overlay-v0.4.0, bios-v0.4.0, ace-v0.4.0, mesh-v0.4.0, vram-v0.4.0, fan-v0.3.0, wdriver-v0.3.0, cec-v0.4.0, sftp-v0.4.0, package-v0.6.0, ncgui-v0.4.0, rpcs3-v0.4.0, consoles-v1.3.0, shadps4-v0.4.0, decky-v0.4.0, datstation-v1.1.0, ppsspp-v0.4.0, pcsx2-v0.5.0, vita3k-v0.3.0.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 03:24:21

Added. Outside the suite, in the notice below the updates: a newer release of a program an installed app
installs in its newest version (HelixSR in the HelixSR Manager, PCSX2's nightly builds in the PCSX2 Manager), with
its tab and what to do in the app, linked to its tile. It shows what the apps recorded when they last checked
(bc250_core.upstream), and follows when the window is active again. Programs an app pins are not listed: a newer one
comes as an update of the app.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 01:53:59

