Release 0.9.13. Pins hdmi-cec-v0.1.5. app update: hdmi-cec

Changelog: 12-10-2026 06:40:31

The portal no longer asks for the suite checkout when a checkout-only app is installed: it finds it (find_checkout),
from the launcher of an installed checkout tool in ~/.local/bin (Suite Releases records its checkout there), else the
first checkout in the home folder up to three folders deep, hidden folders skipped. It looks at startup, so the tiles
know where they come from. Only when there is none does it ask, first whether to choose a folder at all. Asking for a
folder straight away, at the first install, was not liked on the owner's board (12-10-2026).

Changelog: 12-10-2026 06:18:24

Release 0.9.12. Pins hdmi-cec-v0.1.4, demo-tool-v0.1.4, dependency-checker-v0.1.5. updated demo-tool dependency-
checker and hdmi-cec

Changelog: 12-10-2026 06:12:01

A portal installed from a release installs the checkout-only apps (Suite Releases, BC-250 Installer Tests) too,
instead of showing them greyed with "Needs a checkout". The first time one is installed or removed, it asks for the
suite checkout folder, checks that it is one (apps/, core/, tools/stage_app.py), and remembers it in its state folder
(suite-checkout); a folder that stops being a checkout is forgotten. Sources.apps_checkout is that folder: only the
checkout-only apps use it, so the released apps still install from their pinned releases and the portal is not a local
build. Such an install is recorded as "local", as from a portal of the checkout.

